  "qualification": "Task 21 focused shared-VM evidence only. The ten web-stream-bridge fixtures pass on shared VM and local Node v26.10.0. The timer identity, scheduler, process-emitter diagnostic, and 38-case framework-core selections pass on the shared VM; the focused timer/process and EventEmitter fixtures also pass on local Node. test-process-emit.js remains unclassified in the Node inventory, so it earns no Task 22 credit. This report does not qualify the full implemented-Node inventory or Stage A.",
  "adopted_design": "Readable pull state records started, pulling and pullAgain so start settles before pulling, one pull runs at a time, and concurrent demand triggers one recheck. Readable phase remains the terminal authority; queues and pending reads remain FIFO data. Writable algorithms are captured once; start receives a controller whose error transition shares the stream phase. The operation tail begins with start settlement, then serializes writes, close and abort; sync throws and promise rejections enter the same errored transition. Node stream finished routes terminal completion through listener cleanup; addAbortSignal delegates stream-side completion to finished's observation instead of treating any one Duplex event as terminal. stream/promises is projected from the shared stream module so require aliases reuse the same functions and state. Rx.NET contributes only the one-shot pairing of terminal notification with cleanup; WHATWG defines stream ordering. Shared process event keys use one map with string contents or rooted Symbol identity; event-count projection derives from its distinct keys. Scheduler wait/yield runs through the same existing timer and job queues.",
